# A real LUKS2 container (Argon2id key slot), written by cryptsetup -- not built by this project.
# From qnxprobe's tests/fixtures, as carried in the comparison tool's tests/fixtures
# (2026.5.7), MIT -- fme/vendor/LICENSE-gleapp. Its key or passphrase was
# made for the fixture and opens nothing else.
#
# The expected answer, from how it was made: one LUKS2 container, locked; passphrase
# "correct horse battery staple"; an ext4 file system inside.
# Without its key (this program does not ask for one) a run must say the
# volume is LUKS2-encrypted and locked, and that this is not an empty
# disk -- tests/test_real_encrypted_volumes.py.
